**Observation, not fixed (outside my file scope)** — `score-command-transcripts.mjs` line matcher misses a name wrapped in backticks. Verified against the regex itself:

| line | matched |
|---|---|
| `- **COMMAND: /create:readme → started**` | yes |
| `` `COMMAND: /create:readme → started` `` | yes |
| `` COMMAND: `/create:readme` → started `` | **no** |

So the module's own comment ("a model marks it up as a list item, a bold run or a code span") holds only when the span wraps the whole token, not the name. A real reply that code-spans the command name would go uncounted in the `COMMAND:` line rate. No test encodes either behaviour — say the word if you want that shape accepted, it needs a change in `S`.

